    "text": "Pakistan secures its first-ever tuna quota! 🐟\nAccording to Business Recorder, Federal Minister for Maritime Affairs Muhammad Junaid Anwar Chaudhry said Pakistan has secured a tuna quota of 25,000 metric tonnes from the Indian Ocean Tuna Commission for the first time: 15,000 tonnes of yellowfin and 10,000 tonnes of skipjack. He said the quota could generate around $200 million in export earnings. Meeting a Maldivian delegation led by Tourism and Civil Aviation Minister Mohamed Ameen, he invited the Maldives to invest in Pakistan's tuna-processing and canning industry. A high-level Pakistani delegation is due to visit the Maldives in December.\nCan Pakistan's seafood exports grow from here? Tell us below 👇\n\nImage: AI-generated illustration.\n\n#RiseUpPakistan #TunaQuota #BlueEconomy #Exports #PakistanNews",
